Does SWEBOK v4.0a's construction definition include verification, tests and debugging, and establish fixed process boundaries?

Use these exact pinned knowledge graph excerpts and say what they do not prove:
{"claim":{"id":"se:CLM-07B-SWEBOK-CONSTRUCTION-DEFINITION","statement":"SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA4 defines software construction as the detailed creation and maintenance of software through coding, verification, unit testing, integration testing and debugging; states that much design work is performed during construction; and states that boundaries among design, construction and testing, if any, vary depending on the software life cycle processes used.","scope":"SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 4 Introduction (printed page 4-1); generally accepted KA content, not a universal process prescription.","limitations":"The definition deliberately leaves the design/construction/testing boundary life-cycle dependent; it does not fix one process decomposition."},"evidence":{"id":"se:EVD-07B-SWEBOK-CONSTRUCTION-DEFINITION","statement":"SWEBOK v4.0a KA4 defines software construction as the detailed creation and maintenance of software through coding, verification, unit testing, integration testing and debugging; states the KA is linked to all other KAs but most strongly to Software Design (much design work is performed during construction) and Software Testing (engineers unit-test and integration-test throughout construction); and notes that boundaries among design, construction and testing, if any, vary depending on the software life cycle processes used in a project.","limitations":"The Introduction describes linkages between knowledge areas, not measured coupling between activities."},"locator":{"id":"se:LOC-07B-SWEBOK-KA4-INTRO-FUNDAMENTALS","section":"SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 4 Software Construction, Introduction and section 1 Software Construction Fundamentals, including 1.1 Minimizing Complexity, 1.2 Anticipating and Embracing Change, 1.3 Constructing for Verification, 1.4 Reusing Assets and 1.5 Applying Standards in Construction; PDF page indices 98-101; printed pages 4-1 to 4-4"},"source":{"id":"se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A","title":"Guide to the Software Engineering Body of Knowledge (SWEBOK Guide), Version 4.0a","limitations":["A guide to the body of knowledge, not the complete body of knowledge","Generally accepted knowledge is not a uniform prescription for every project","Its topic citations are not comprehensive","Related disciplines are identified but not characterized in full"]}}
